    <briefdescription>
<para>Tree iterator. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Points to an element in tree. There are 4 possible states of iterator: 1)Normal. Points to concrete element in tree. 2)Invalid. Points to nothing. Safe. 3)Broken. Normal can become broken during tree modification. Safe to use, but has undefined behavior. 4)Uninitialized (or initialized in wrong way). Unsafe and undefined behaviour. </para>    </detaileddescription>
